        "difficulty": "easy"
      },
      {
        "questionText": "How are algebraic fractions added or subtracted?",
        "options": [],
        "correctAnswer": "By finding a common denominator (LCM) then combining the numerators.",
        "explanation": "For example x/2 + x/3 = 5x/6.",
        "difficulty": "easy"
      },
      {
